  "question": {
    "text": "During an adiabatic process, the pressure of a gas is found to be proportional to the cube of its absolute temperature. The ratio <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></msub><msub><mi>C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></msub></mfrac></math>&nbsp; for the gas is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac bevelled=\"true\"><mn>4</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac bevelled=\"true\"><mn>5</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac bevelled=\"true\"><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "In an adiabatic process, <math> <mrow> <msup> <mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">T</mtext> <mi>γ</mi> </msup> <mo>=</mo> <mfenced close=\")\" open=\"(\" separators=\",\"> <mrow> <mtext>constant</mtext> </mrow> </mfenced> <msup> <mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">P</mtext> <mrow> <mi>γ</mi> <mo>-</mo> <mn>1</mn> </mrow> </msup> </mrow> </math><br />or&nbsp;&nbsp;<math>&nbsp; <mrow> <msup> <mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">T</mtext> <mrow> <mi>γ</mi> <mo>/</mo> <mi>γ</mi> <mo>-</mo> <mn>1</mn> </mrow> </msup> <mo>=</mo> <mfenced close=\")\" open=\"(\" separators=\",\"> <mrow> <mtext>constant</mtext> </mrow></mfenced><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">&nbsp;P</mtext> </mrow> </math><br /><br />Given&nbsp;<math> <mrow> <msup> <mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">T</mtext> <mn>3</mn> </msup> <mo>=</mo> <mfenced close=\")\" open=\"(\" separators=\",\"> <mrow> <mtext>constant</mtext> </mrow> </mfenced> <mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">&nbsp;P</mtext> </mrow> </math><br /><br /><math> <mrow> <mo>∴</mo> </mrow> </math>&nbsp;&nbsp;<math> <mrow> <mfrac> <mrow> <mi>γ</mi> </mrow> <mrow> <mi>γ</mi> <mo>-</mo> <mn>1</mn> </mrow> </mfrac> <mo>=</mo> <mn>3</mn> <mo>⇒</mo> <mn>3</mn> <mi>γ</mi> <mo>-</mo> <mn>3</mn> <mo>=</mo> <mi>γ</mi> </mrow> </math><br /><br />or&nbsp;&nbsp;<math>&nbsp; <mrow> <mn>2</mn> <mi>γ</mi> <mo>=</mo> <mn>3</mn> <mo>⇒</mo> <mi>γ</mi> <mo>=</mo> <mn>3</mn> <mo>/</mo> <mn>2</mn></mrow></math><br /><br />For monoatomic gas, <math> <mrow> <mi>γ</mi> <mo>=</mo> <mfrac> <mrow> <mn>5</mn> </mrow> <mrow> <mn>3</mn> </mrow> </mfrac> </mrow> </math> = 1.67<br /><br />For diatomic gas, <math> <mrow> <mi>γ</mi> <mo>=</mo> <mfrac> <mrow> <mn>7</mn> </mrow> <mrow> <mn>5</mn> </mrow> </mfrac> </mrow> </math> = 1.4<br /><br />when <math> <mrow> <mi>γ</mi> </mrow> </math> = 1.5, the gas must be a suitable mixture of monoatomic and diatomic gases<br /><br /><math> <mrow> <mo>∴</mo> </mrow> </math>&nbsp;&nbsp;<math>&nbsp;&nbsp; <mrow> <mi>γ</mi> </mrow> </math> = 3/2."
  }
